# Raid conditions and late deployment.
ts-phase-day = Day
ts-phase-evening = Evening
ts-phase-night = Night
ts-conditions-title = Time of day: { $phase }
ts-conditions-day = Good visibility. Less loot and fewer enemies. Suitable for cautious supply runs.
ts-conditions-evening = Dusk. Moderate loot value, reinforced patrols and more creatures. Bring a flashlight.
ts-conditions-night = Low visibility. Valuable loot, numerous guards and creatures. Bring a flashlight and spare ammunition.
ts-raid-existing = A raid is in progress. { $time } remaining. You will join this map at a random location; loot and timer will not reset.
ts-raid-next = The next departure creates one shared 15-minute raid. It ends early when every participant has left.
ts-ready-join = Join the active raid
tarkov-error-landing = No clear landing spot was found. Try departing again.

# Rules precede character creation.
ts-rules-title = TarkovStation / Entry rules
ts-rule-1 = 1. Don't be a jerk. Respect other players. The hub is a peaceful area.
ts-rule-2 = 2. Toxicity is not welcome. Insults and harassment do not make the game more enjoyable.
ts-rule-3 = 3. Cheats and third-party software used for an unfair advantage are prohibited. Violations result in a permanent ban.
ts-rule-4 = 4. We do not present ourselves as a Roleplay project, but follow LRP boundaries. You do not have to roleplay every action or fear for your character's life. Discuss out-of-character information in LOOC, not the general in-game chat.
ts-rule-5 = 5. ERP is prohibited.
ts-rules-gameplay = Raid alliances rely on trust. Any player, including your faction or party members, may attack. Death loses the equipment you brought into the raid; your stash remains. The shared ten-hour cycle ends with rankings and a character and property wipe.
ts-rules-agreement = I have read the rules and agree to follow them.
ts-rules-continue = Agree and create a character
ts-discord = Our Discord server

